# nr-office-author-docx-build: the Word HTML builder and runner of crate mixdog-office-author. What the lead applies (all of it is
# in files this task does not own). It was not compiled by this task (no cargo run).

## 0. What must exist first: the docx batch dispatcher of nr-office-ooxml-docx-edits
docx_build.rs makes the page, the document font, the styles and the running lines with ONE call:

    use mixdog_ooxml::docx::apply_docx;
    apply_docx(&mut zip, &operations)?;      // zip: &mut mixdog_ooxml::zipio::Package, operations: &[serde_json::Value]

`apply_docx` is the port of `applyDocx(zip, operations)` of portable-docx.mjs (nr-office-ooxml-docx-edits owns it and
`docx_edits.rs`, which holds `set_header_footer` and `add_page_numbers`; the plan names the module `docx.rs`). The operations
this task sends are `set_page`, `set_document_font`, `define_styles`, `set_header_footer` and `add_page_numbers` (the
`docx_operations` ones exist in the tree; the last two exist only after that task). If the dispatcher is named or shaped
otherwise, change the one `use` line and the one call in `docx_build::build_docx_from_flow`; nothing else depends on it. This
task wrote no second implementation of the two running-line operations.
Node's `applyPortableOoxmlBatch` also ran `refreshDocxTableOfContents` after the batch; the blank document this builds has no
table of contents, so it is not called here (if the dispatcher exposes the whole batch as one function, that call may be used).

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-author/src/lib.rs
Beside `pub mod pptx_html_runner;` add:

    pub mod docx_build;
    pub mod docx_html_runner;

and extend the crate doc by one sentence: `docx_build` is the Word HTML builder (`authoring/docx-html-build.mjs`: the flow
`measure_docx` read from the browser becomes WordprocessingML written block by block on the portable writer) and
`docx_html_runner` the Word HTML runner (`authoring/docx-html-runner.mjs`: measure, photograph the captures, print the same HTML
as the review reference, build, keep `<document>.mixdog-source.html` and the page images of the print).

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-author/Cargo.toml
[dependencies], one new edge between workspace crates (keep the list's order; mixdog-office-pdf is a workspace dependency and
the crate does not depend on mixdog-office-author, so there is no cycle):

    mixdog-office-pdf = { workspace = true }

Used for `render_pdf_pages` (the page images of the browser's print, `renderPdfPages(print, { maxWidth: 900 })`).
Every other crate the two modules and the twin test use (base64, serde_json, url, mixdog-core-api, mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js,
mixdog-office-base, mixdog-ooxml, mixdog-fonts, mixdog-rt; dev: async-trait, tokio, mixdog-testkit, mixdog-rt with test-support)
is in the manifest already. Cargo.lock gains the edge (`cargo update --workspace --offline`); mixdog-workspace-hack: only if
hakari asks.

## 3. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json (the index of the fixture sets)
Add this entry in its place in the list sorted by `set` (where the sorted order puts `office-docx-build`, before
`office-docx-operations`):

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-docx-build.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-docx-build/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "b8358e668d2abab507905d92a4ee71a2342e69b0fa1873815c6aafe87a5ab4cf",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-docx-build.mjs",
      "set": "office-docx-build",
      "totalBytes": 293092
    },

(Recomputed from the committed office-docx-build/MANIFEST.json and golden.json if the tool that keeps the index reformats them.
Recorded from the product tree at C:/Project/mixdog, which is not an exact commit export, so `product.commit` is null like the
other office sets. The set is in this task's commit, added with `git add --sparse`.)

## 4. SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)
No name to remove: this task registers no service and adds no protocol method.

## 5. What the later tasks take from this one
- The author action (the office worker's `author` route for `.docx`) calls
  `mixdog_office_author::docx_html_runner::run_docx_html_authoring(endpoint, tokens, registry, note, html, output, DocxRunOptions::new(target))`
  and gets Node's result object (`ok`, `output`, `bytes`, `kit: "html"`, `htmlSource`, `htmlPages: [{ page, path }]`, `logs`,
  `elapsedMs`; or `{ ok: false, error: { message }, elapsedMs }`; a cancellation is `Err(RunError::Cancelled)`).
  `docx_html_artifacts(target)` names the kept files (`source()`, `print()`, `compare(page)`).
- The recording of this set has no `runs` section (the recorder needs a browser for it; run it with `--browser` on a machine
  that has one, then `twin_live_docx_build` and the ignored `html_run_*` tests check Rust against the same browser).
- The Node tests of `office-docx-html.slow.test.mjs` that go through the whole `author`/`qa`/`finalize` action (the session,
  `render.compare`, the review token, the unscored finalize, the untouched neighbour file, `open` of a refused path) belong to
  the author action; the runner-level ones are ported as `html_run_*` tests and `twin_docx_build`.
